1
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,097
Just ten more minutes.

2
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,540
Maybe five. Wake up! Now!

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,710
Sugu?

4
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,640
Would you get up already?

5
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,220
It's 5.30.

6
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,858
Even though you're a lost
child to Vecta and a guest,

7
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,413
you're still expected to get up on time.

8
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:47,910
Okay.

9
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,877
So let's

10
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:13,960
do

11
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:21,890
this.

12
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:24,057
I'm living in the darkness.

13
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:34,970
I'm feeling it.

14
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:35,883
Yourself.

15
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:42,037
I'm having a love song. I'm watching it.

16
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,591
I'm seeing it on the day.

17
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:49,657
Shiny summer diamond I'm feeling it.
Let's go to the beginning of the world.

18
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,500
Let's dive into the rocket's orbit!

19
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:56,197
Let's dive into the light.

20
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,110
Let's dive into the sky?

21
00:01:57,193 --> 00:01:58,460
What time do you think?

22
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,477
I'm here to come.

23
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,457
I have to think about taking place.

24
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,737
Let's go to the end of the world.

25
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,117
On the end of the world.

26
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:40,040
There's a lot I don't understand about
this place, but I know I'm gonna need.

27
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,337
Eugeo's help to get to Senator.

28
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:46,200
Thing is, I have to get him
out of his Calling first.

29
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,541
And to do that, we'll have
to chop this tree down.

30
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:52,720
What was that? Huh? Oh, nothing.

31
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:55,157
We're all done with the morning's quota.

32
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:56,416
It's time for lunch.

33
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,320
I'm starving.

34
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,120
You know what I wish?

35
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:07,182
I wish you could have
tasted the pies Alice made.

36
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:10,598
The crust was so flaky and
there was so much filling.

37
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,648
Having it with some
fresh milk was the best.

38
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,537
There's nothing in the world
that tasted better than that.

39
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,620
Was that Alice's calling? A baker?

40
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:21,980
No, not even.

41
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:25,857
Back in those days, she was studying
the sacred arts at the church.

42
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:28,940
She was the greatest prodigy
this village ever had.

43
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:32,177
She could cast all kinds of
spells by the time she was ten.

44
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,090
Wow.

45
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:36,597
What's up with the girl
living at the church?

46
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,820
You know, Selka?

47
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,477
Oh, she's Alice's little sister.

48
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,660
After Alice was taken away,

49
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,160
Selka moved to the church to become
a nun and study the sacred arts.

50
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,617
There's a bunch of kids there, too.

51
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,897
Are they there for the same reason as her?

52
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:57,137
They lost their parents to the plague
that hit the village three years ago.

53
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,980
The church is the only place that
had room for them. Poor kids.

54
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,133
It's like we're cursed.

55
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,537
All these strange things
have been happening lately.

56
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:09,537
Like people being attacked and
kidnapped down the main road.

57
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:12,444
The villagers say goblins
are the ones doing it.

58
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,075
There's goblins here?

59
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,967
I have a feeling all
that talk's just rumors.

60
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:22,202
If it were true, an Integrity Knight should
have come by now to put a stop to them.

61
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,421
They'd have been here in a flash.

62
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:28,097
Like when Alice touched the
ground in the Dark Territory.

63
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:30,480
That was nothing compared to goblins.

64
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:33,120
No, it's not. Either way,

65
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:37,957
there have been a lot of deaths over the
past two or three years, more than usual.

66
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,334
Can't you revive them?

67
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:42,149
You know, like with
one of the sacred arts?

68
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,680
Well, I don't know about that,

69
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:48,577
but I remember Alice saying
there was a high-level

70
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,297
sacred art that could stop
a life from decreasing.

71
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,860
That'd be a good one to know, I guess.

72
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,290
It would.

73
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,477
Alice said she found a passage about that

74
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,017
spell in one of the old
books in the church.

75
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:04,335
But the problem is, only the high
priest at the Axiom Church can use it.

76
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,390
Axiom Church?

77
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,880
It's in Senator.

78
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,537
They wrote the Taboo Index.

79
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:12,149
But, like, do you have to be a
high priest to use the spell?

80
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,948
Maybe someone like you
or me could learn it.

81
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,460
No, it's not for regular folk like us.

82
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:22,297
The arts get their strength
from the sacred power

83
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:25,615
that Solus and Terraria
saturate the air and land with.

84
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,951
The more elaborate the art,
the more sacred power it takes.

85
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,957
It would take more power
than this forest has,

86
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,805
and no one from here to
Zakaria could wield it.

87
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:39,857
That's too bad I wonder
if there's a sacred

88
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,705
art that could help us
to chop this thing down.

89
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:48,717
That would make things easier there's
gotta be something better than this.

90
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:54,897
Oh hey Yugio is there anything
tougher than this in your village?

91
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,697
No I'm afraid not the only thing.

92
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,717
Stronger than the dragon
bone axe would be an

93
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:04,420
integrity night on second
thought maybe there is.

94
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:07,360
Wait here for me.

95
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,814
I'll be back in a bit.

96
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:09,770
Huh?

97
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,040
Whoa, you okay?

98
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:26,720
Mind if I open it?

99
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,070
Okay.

100
00:06:29,153 --> 00:06:29,983
Just be careful.

101
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:34,141
If it falls on your foot, it'll
leave you with more than a scratch.

102
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:52,160
No way.

103
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,440
It's the blue rose sword
from the fairy tale.

104
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,100
What fairy tale?

105
00:06:57,380 --> 00:06:58,660
It goes like this.

106
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:02,517
300 years ago, Bercouli the
swordsman went to the End Mountains.

107
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:07,740
He entered the lair of the white dragon,
our protector, and found that sword.

108
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,540
It's just a silly story.

109
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:16,220
That is, it was, until some kids
decided to find out if it was true.

110
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:18,200
I mentioned it yesterday.

111
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:19,950
Remember?

112
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:22,657
About how Alice and I
went to the End Mountains?

113
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:25,160
I found that sword in the dragon's lair.

114
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:28,940
I couldn't even lift it by
myself back then. Really?

115
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,517
What'd the dragon have to say about
you guys breaking into its home?

116
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,365
There was nothing left
of it except some bones.

117
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:39,774
We took the wrong tunnel, and then
Alice crossed into the Dark Territory.

118
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,180
And then she was taken away.

119
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,900
I couldn't do anything for
her except stand there.

120
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:52,620
I wanted to save her, but my
arms and legs were frozen.

121
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:54,560
I'm sorry.

122
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:56,039
Back to the sword.

123
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:59,480
I left it there that
day and never forgot it.

124
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:01,680
So two summers ago, I went back.

125
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,257
Every day of rest, I'd go drag it.

126
00:08:04,340 --> 00:08:06,577
It took three months to get it back here.

127
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,013
It took you three whole months to do it?

128
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:11,114
Why'd you even bother?

129
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:15,406
I guess I was hoping one day I'd
have the strength to swing it.

130
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,344
I'm still not strong enough to.

131
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,215
Do you think you are?

132
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,640
I'm down to try.

133
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,488
I'm a swordsman, after all.

134
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:35,274
Looks like it's too heavy for you, too.

135
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:39,900
It's not made of steel, or is it?

136
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,640
No, I don't think so.

137
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:44,291
And it's not silver or dragon bone either.

138
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,600
I think it might be a
divine object. Of what?

139
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:50,357
It's something that was either made with

140
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:53,160
the help of the gods
or was created by them.

141
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,700
We call things like that divine objects.

142
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,920
That makes sense.

143
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:02,700
Hey, Eugeo, could you, like, check
how much life the Giga Cedar has now?

144
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:03,650
Don't tell me.

145
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:04,563
Let me guess.

146
00:09:04,646 --> 00:09:06,957
You're going to try
striking it with the sword.

147
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,628
You're damn straight, I am.

148
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,837
Unless the Taboo Index forbids it.

149
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,685
But I bet it doesn't, does it?

150
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,180
No, it doesn't. It's funny.

151
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,048
All this seems so familiar.

152
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:25,960
Right now, it's at 232,315.

153
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,350
Cool.

154
00:09:27,433 --> 00:09:28,263
Remember that.

155
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,540
Did you hurt yourself?

156
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:51,860
No, I'm okay.

157
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,660
I told you before, that tree is tough.

158
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,540
No way.

159
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:00,920
You actually cut into it.

160
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:07,160
And deep, too. Go on.

161
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:09,140
See where its life's at now.

162
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,490
Oh, right.

163
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:15,437
2-30-2-3-14.

164
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,500
You're kidding.

165
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,800
It only went down one point?

166
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:21,380
Your hit landed in the wrong spot.

167
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,617
I bet it would have decreased
its life a lot more if

168
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,935
you got it in the center of
the cut instead of the bark

169
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,097
Looks like your intuition was right.

170
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:33,437
The sword is more effective
than the axe Even so

171
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,497
we'd have to master using
it to get any results.

172
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:38,060
I can't hit it straight,

173
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:42,457
but I bet you could I can barely
hold the sword let alone swing it.

174
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:45,716
It's all about technique and
I can help you with that.

175
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:49,231
Okay I'll give it a shot.

176
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,200
It's... so heavy.

177
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:59,017
First thing, find your balance.

178
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,877
And when you swing, swing with your body.

179
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,117
With swords, it's more about
momentum, not just arm strength.

180
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,030
Mm-hmm.

181
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,110
Whoa!

182
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,900
Hey, you all right?

183
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:30,460
I think I lost some life on that one.

184
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,920
Oh, well, it was a good try.

185
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:45,840
If durability's life, I lost
some when I took a swing.

186
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:50,057
Hmm, it says my object
control authority's at 38.

187
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:52,020
I guess that's my parameter.

188
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,940
The sword is higher.

189
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,525
That's what I'm talking about.

190
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:09,420
At this rate, I'll never get to Senator.

191
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:14,120
I need Eugeo's help, but he
won't bail on his calling.

192
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:19,520
If it wasn't for that taboo index,
he could do whatever he wants.

193
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:22,700
He said the Axiom Church came up with it.

194
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:25,140
Wonder what the deal is with them.

195
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:30,000
If I'm right and these people are AI
Fluctlights in a simulated civilization,

196
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:33,616
there's no way the system
would let them break a rule.

197
00:12:35,340 --> 00:12:36,200
Hang on.

198
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:39,457
Yu-Gi-Oh said Alice broke
the Taboo Index when

199
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:42,157
she accidentally crossed
into the Dark Territory.

200
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,320
But she was there by choice.

201
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:47,300
She went against the system.

202
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:50,860
So is she not an AI? Hello?

203
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:52,476
Is someone in there?

204
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:53,920
Yeah, there is.

205
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,520
I'm almost done.

206
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:57,280
Oh, um, no.

207
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,937
You can take your time.

208
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:00,196
I was just checking.

209
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,536
Sorry to bother you.

210
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:02,650
Good night.

211
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:03,563
Uh, Selka!

212
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,720
I wanted to ask you something.

213
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,360
So, what was it you wanted to ask me?

214
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:20,770
Yeah.

215
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,620
Um, it's about your older sister.

216
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:33,060
I heard about her, you
know, from Yu-Gi-Oh.

217
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:36,480
And, like, he told me her name was Alice.

218
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,840
He did, did he?

219
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:41,337
What else did he tell you
besides her name was Alice?

220
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:45,540
Oh, um, he said she was studying
the sacred arts here at the church.

221
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,260
And how six years ago an
Integrity Knight took her.

222
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:52,184
I got the feeling he's
really worried about her.

223
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,660
I didn't know.

224
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,960
I thought he forgot about her.

225
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:59,295
This explains a lot about him, though.

226
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,820
She's the reason Eugeo's so sad.

227
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,180
I didn't get that.

228
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:05,440
He seems fine. He's not.

229
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,288
You had to have noticed it.

230
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,220
How quiet and gloomy he is.

231
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:10,540
Oh, yeah.

232
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,260
When my sister was here,

233
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:16,682
every time I saw him, he
had a smile on his face.

234
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:20,435
I don't remember ever seeing
him without one back then.

235
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:21,980
But not anymore.

236
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,937
He spends his days of rest alone,

237
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:28,432
and the only time I see him
is when he goes to the forest.

238
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,240
Selka, you really like him, don't you?

239
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:33,950
Ah!

240
00:14:34,033 --> 00:14:35,680
I didn't say that! Oh my gosh!

241
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,005
Everyone compares me to Alice.

242
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,848
No one says it, but I know.

243
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:46,340
When my parents see me,
I remind them of her.

244
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,520
And I can't stand it anymore.

245
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,637
That's probably why Eugeo avoids me.

246
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:56,480
When he sees me, he thinks of her
and I can tell it makes him sad.

247
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,260
But there's nothing I can do.

248
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,200
It's not my fault she's gone.

249
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:08,677
I'm sorry, I'm acting like a baby.

250
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:10,597
No, not at all.

251
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,177
It's good to cry.

252
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:14,340
It's better than holding it in.

253
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,640
Yes, you're right.

254
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:20,337
In fact, I feel much better already.

255
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:23,540
Crying in front of others
is not something I do.

256
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:25,490
Really?

257
00:15:25,573 --> 00:15:26,637
You're tougher than I am.

258
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:30,367
I can't tell you how many times
I've cried in front of people.

259
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:32,600
Hold on.

260
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,860
Is your memory back? No!

261
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,905
It just feels that way is all.

262
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,240
Anyway, back to you.

263
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,377
It doesn't matter what anyone thinks.

264
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,400
You're you, not your sister.

265
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:46,340
You can only live your
life, not someone else's.

266
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:48,620
Yes, you're right.

267
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:53,660
I should get going.

268
00:15:56,420 --> 00:16:01,580
Say, did Eugeo happen to tell you why
the Integrity Knight took my sister away?

269
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:04,300
Um, yeah, he did.

270
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,167
My parents wouldn't tell me.

271
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,380
And Eugeo wouldn't tell me either.

272
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:12,300
Maybe you could tell me why? Yeah, sure.

273
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:17,804
She went to the End Mountains, then touched
the ground on the Dark Territory side.

274
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,300
I see.

275
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,020
The End Mountains, huh?

276
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,608
Tomorrow's our day of rest.

277
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:27,880
Still, be on time.

278
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:30,417
I won't be coming to wake you up anymore.

279
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,206
Okay, I'll keep that in mind.

280
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,780
Good morning.

281
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,840
Oh, good morning.

282
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:53,940
By chance.

283
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,620
Have you seen Selka today? No.

284
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,371
I just woke up, actually.

285
00:16:58,740 --> 00:16:59,620
So I see.

286
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:02,215
Well, I have not seen her all morning.

287
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:05,377
She missed prayers, and
she is not in her room.

288
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:07,060
I am worried.

289
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:09,737
She would never leave
without telling me first.

290
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,114
I'm sure she's around.

291
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:12,260
I hope so.

292
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:15,580
If you see her, please
let me know. Yes, ma 'am.

293
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,880
Yujiu! Hey, Kirito.

294
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,866
Have you seen Selka anywhere?

295
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:23,440
I haven't. Why?

296
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,296
Sister Azalea's been looking for her.

297
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:28,617
She says she left without telling her.

298
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,582
That's strange.

299
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:31,277
Well, I'm trying to find her.

300
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,837
Do you know where she could have gone?

301
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,180
No, she and I haven't spoken in ages.

302
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:38,368
Do you think something
might have upset her?

303
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,100
I see.

304
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,900
The End Mountains, huh?

305
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,350
Oh, man.

306
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:47,317
Last night, I told her
what happened to Alice.

307
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:50,106
At least everything you
told me that happened.

308
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:54,451
She wouldn't go to the End
Mountains on her own, would she?

309
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,477
That's exactly where she went!

310
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,325
We have to bring her back now!

311
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:07,170
What's wrong?

312
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,260
It's been stepped on.

313
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:14,160
It's lost a bit of life.

314
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,757
Someone's been by here, and
it wasn't that long ago.

315
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,337
Then we're on the right track.

316
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,657
That's gotta be Selka.

317
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,570
Yeah.

318
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,120
Well, this is it.

319
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,880
No way.

320
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,040
It really is the end.

321
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,700
When I first came here,
I thought the same thing.

322
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:41,300
And the dark territory's
down that way, huh? Yeah.

323
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,560
Are you ready?

324
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:44,740
Yeah, I think. I guess.

325
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,220
System call.

326
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,060
Generate luminous elements.

327
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:50,570
Adhere.

328
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:54,080
Yu-Gi-Oh, what'd you do?

329
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,620
It's a sacred art.

330
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:57,622
An easy one that anybody can do.

331
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:59,660
But, like, you said system.

332
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,497
Do you even know what that means?

333
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:02,410
Nothing.

334
00:19:02,493 --> 00:19:03,323
It's just a word.

335
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,441
Well, a command.

336
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,351
It's to call on the gods.

337
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:10,177
As long as you have enough skill, you'll
be blessed with the art you summon.

338
00:19:10,260 --> 00:19:12,600
He thinks he's casting a magic spell.

339
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,640
Come on, let's go. Right.

340
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,200
Maybe she didn't come in here.

341
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:27,284
I mean, there's no sign of her.

342
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,280
This is as good a sign as any.

343
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,320
It could be her, I guess.

344
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:41,420
Hey, Yujiya. What is it?

345
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:44,014
If she crosses into the Dark Territory,

346
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,177
does an Integrity Knight
come and take her right away?

347
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,200
No, not until the next day.

348
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:53,960
He'll fly to the village and arrest
her there, just like six years ago.

349
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:59,184
Then, even if we're too late, we still
have a chance to keep him from getting her.

350
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:02,760
But that would be interfering. We can't.

351
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:04,460
Of course we can.

352
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:07,587
Look, even if she does
break the taboo index,

353
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:10,117
all we have to do is keep
her away from the village.

354
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:13,671
The Integrity Knight can't
arrest her if he can't find her.

355
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,197
That's insane.

356
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,780
We can't hide forever.

357
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:18,537
And I have my calling.

358
00:20:18,620 --> 00:20:20,740
But I don't, so I can take her away.

359
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:25,177
If I didn't say anything,
she wouldn't be in this mess.

360
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,380
This is all on me.

361
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,260
No, it's not.

362
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,800
Sugou!

363
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,720
That way!

364
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,800
Take cover!

365
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:01,720
Crap. Goblins.

366
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,310
Sugou!

367
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:13,800
What are you doing?

368
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:23,220
Looky, looky.

369
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:28,140
Two more white Eum Brassy Brats
just a-wandering around. Yummy!

370
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:30,424
Let's tie him to the other one!

371
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:33,290
Silence!

372
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,160
They're male youths.

373
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:38,880
We take them back, no one buy them.

374
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,270
Worthless.

375
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:42,640
Kill them and make them meat instead.

376
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:46,370
Eugeo!

377
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:51,090
Eugeo?

378
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:55,930
Eugeo!

379
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:58,760
Yu-Gi-Oh!

380
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:02,237
Yu-Gi-Oh!

381
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:03,500
Oh...

382
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:27,777
If you're bright, I'll
see the sun in the sky.

383
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:31,657
I'll see the sun in the morning.

384
00:22:57,900 --> 00:23:00,800
For my tears, when I'm out of my tears,

385
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:04,897
I'm not a pain.

386
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:09,117
It's not your eyes.

387
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,420
I'm not a pain.

388
00:23:14,020 --> 00:23:16,520
If you're my body, I'm feeling it.

389
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:24,280
It's a pain that I've felt, I'll
be able to give you some pain.

390
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:38,080
Next time, Departure.
